From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winex11: a restarted shell's desktop is shown when it gets the
 dead one's window id

After the shell died (an xkill'ed Linux window took explorer with it, David
2026-10-02), the restarted shell made a new X window for the desktop -- and
the X server, giving a new client the ids a gone one had, gave it the dead
window's id. 0755's "the desktop's window is gone" check compared the two,
found them the same and left the desktop as it was: no window data for it,
never mapped. Under the compositor's window manager only the backdrop was
seen until a reboot.

- the remembered window being this shell's new one (the same id) is a dead
  one too: the desktop gets the new window;
- the new window is mapped there: the desktop is visible already, and no
  show is coming to map it.

Test: test/shellrestart-gate.sh restarts the shell a second time with no
other X client between (where the X server may reuse the ids) and checks the
desktop is on the screen (mutant SG_MUTANT_REUSED_ID_ALIVE fails it; the
map's mutant only shows under a window manager). Verified on the installed system's
compositor (QA VM): explorer killed, desktop and Start back.
---
--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
@@ -2672,7 +2672,17 @@
     else
     {
         Window win = (Window)NtUserGetProp( hwnd, whole_window_prop );
-        if (win && win != root_window && is_virtual_desktop() && !desktop_window_exists( win ))
+        /* the dead shell's window id can be this shell's new window's too:
+         * the X server gives a new client the ids a gone one had (Xwayland
+         * did, after explorer was killed), and "the same window" was taken
+         * for alive -- the desktop got no window and was never shown */
+        if (win && is_virtual_desktop() &&
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_REUSED_ID_ALIVE
+            (win == root_window ||
+#else
+            (0 ||
+#endif
+             !desktop_window_exists( win )))
         {
             /* Stained Glass OS: the desktop outlived the shell that made its
              * X window -- a program still running on it (a crashed one kept
@@ -2685,6 +2695,18 @@
             WARN( "desktop window %lx is gone, using %lx\n", win, root_window );
 #ifndef SG_MUTANT_STALE_DESKTOP
             create_desktop_win_data( root_window, hwnd );
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_RESTART_UNMAPPED
+            /* the desktop is visible already (the dead shell showed it): no
+             * show is coming to map this new window -- after a shell's crash
+             * only the backdrop was seen, under the compositor's window
+             * manager (Xvfb, with none, showed it anyway) */
+            if (NtUserGetWindowLongW( hwnd, GWL_STYLE ) & WS_VISIBLE)
+            {
+                Display *display = x11drv_thread_data()->display;
+                XMapWindow( display, root_window );
+                XFlush( display );
+            }
+#endif
             return;
 #endif
         }
